Here is the complete example.
```javascript
function chooseIndex(sample, size) {
  if (!Number.isFinite(sample) || sample < 0 || sample >= 1) return null;
  if (!Number.isInteger(size) || size < 1 || size > 1000) return null;
  return Math.min(size - 1, Math.floor(sample * size));
}
console.log(Math.floor(-1.2));
console.log(Math.ceil(-1.2));
console.log(chooseIndex(0.5, 4));
const sample = Math.random();
console.log(sample >= 0 && sample < 1);
```
Output:
```text
-2
-1
2
true
```
With four choices, the positions are 0, 1, 2, and 3. A sample of 0.5 gives position 2.
